==English==

===Verb===
'''to [[rule]] [[out]]'''

# {{transitive}} To cross an item out by drawing a straight line through it, as with a ruler.
# {{idiom|transitive}} To [[reject]] an option from a list of [[possibilities]].
#:''As John Doe had an alibi, the police were able to '''rule''' him '''out''' as a suspect.''
# {{idiom|transitive}} To make something [[impossible]].
#:''The constant rain '''ruled out''' any chance of a game of tennis.''

====Synonyms====
*(''reject''): [[eliminate]], [[reject]]

*(''make impossible''): [[preclude]]

====Antonyms====
*(''reject''): [[consider]], [[rule in]]
*(''make impossible''): [[allow]]

